  "summary": "The M-RED-TEAM campaign compromised the AsyncAPI project via a GitHub Actions 'pwn request' (pull_request_target checking out untrusted PR code), stealing an asyncapi-bot PAT to publish five malicious npm package versions under the @asyncapi namespace. The staged JavaScript payload runs on import, drops sync.js to a NodeJS folder, retrieves an encrypted bundle from IPFS, and installs a modular trojan framework with systemd persistence and multi-channel C2 (HTTP, Nostr, Ethereum, libp2p). It harvests browser credentials, SSH keys, npm/GitHub tokens, AWS credentials, macOS Keychain and crypto wallets.",
